  "body": "Currently the spec says that `new Response(\"\")` and `new Response(new FormData()`) is handled different from `new Response()`. All three generate a Response with an empty body, but the first two also set the `content-type` header.\n\nIs this intentional? Does it really make sense to set the `content-type` header even if no body is set?\n",
